Chapter: TestBoardsScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

 THE SEVENTEENTH GENERATOR ON THE PIPELINE MODEL (PipelineModel.md). The
 emitted script is byte-identical to the one that shipped before the migration.

 THIS SCRIPT GRADES WHICHEVER COMPILER IS ALREADY IN `build-output`. The seed is
 copied to `Stage0` ONLY when `Stage0` is absent, so a stale binary left there
 by an earlier run is used instead, and the board result is then a statement
 about that binary rather than about the seed. `sweep-apps` stages the seed
 UNCONDITIONALLY on the line beside it. Both are shipped, both are on the same
 path, and they disagree. Recorded rather than repaired here, because changing
 the guard changes behaviour and this migration's gate is byte-identity.

 THE FINAL EXIT IS THE FAILURE COUNT, a computed code, which `PipeOutcome`
 cannot spell. That is the second generator to need it after `sweep-apps`, and
 the verdict below is empty rather than false.

Section: Parameters

  testboards-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-choice-default "Arch" ["all", "arm64", "riscv64"] (SeLit "all")]

Section: The pipeline, declared before it is spelled

  repo-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "Repo", pa-kind = PkDir, pa-expr = SeVar "Repo", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "(Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')).Path") }

  renode-exe-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "RenodeExe", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "RenodeExe", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "Get-RenodeExe -Repo $Repo") }

  out-dir-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "OutDir", pa-kind = PkDir, pa-expr = SeVar "OutDir", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'output\\boards'") }

  seed-cdx-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "SeedCdx", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "SeedCdx", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "Join-Path $Repo 'seed\\Codex.cdx'") }

  stage0-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "Stage0", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "Stage0", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "Join-Path $Repo 'build-output\\bare-metal\\Codex.cdx'") }

  hello-src-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "HelloSrc", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "HelloSrc", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "Join-Path $OutDir 'hello-board.codex'") }

 `boards`, `pass`, `fail` AND `skip` ARE BUILT BY RAW STATEMENTS, the three
 tallies by one raw line together, so none declares a production.

  boards-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "boards", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "boards", pa-from = None }

  pass-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "pass", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "pass", pa-from = None }

  fail-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "fail", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "fail", pa-from = None }

  skip-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "skip", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "skip", pa-from = None }

  tb-arts : List PipeArtifact = [repo-art, renode-exe-art, out-dir-art, seed-cdx-art, stage0-art, hello-src-art, boards-art, pass-art, fail-art, skip-art]

Section: S01 -- Preamble

  s01-body : List ShellCmd =
    let skip-renode = [ScRaw "Write-RenodeSkip", ScExit (SeInt 0)]
    in [ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScBlank, pipe-produce repo-art, ScRunDot (SeRaw "(Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'renode-config.ps1')"), pipe-produce renode-exe-art, pipe-produce out-dir-art, ScMkdir (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "OutDir"), ScBlank, pipe-produce seed-cdx-art, pipe-produce stage0-art, ScMkdir (SeRaw "(Split-Path $Stage0)"), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "Stage0"))) [ScCopy (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "SeedCdx") (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "Stage0")] [], ScBlank, ScIf (SeNot (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "RenodeExe")) skip-renode []]

  s01 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "preamble", ps-why = "find Renode, take the output directory, and stage the seed as the compiler ONLY IF build-output holds nothing", ps-in = [], ps-out = [repo-art, renode-exe-art, out-dir-art, seed-cdx-art, stage0-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 0 "Renode is not installed, so every board arm is skipped and the run reports success"], ps-body = s01-body }

Section: S02 -- Hello Source

  s02-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, pipe-produce hello-src-art, ScRaw "@\"\nChapter: Hello\n  cites Foreword chapter Console\nSection: Main\n  opening : [Console] Nothing = act\n    print-line \"BOARD-TEST-OK\"\n  end\n\"@ | Set-Content $HelloSrc -Encoding UTF8"]

  s02 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "hello source", ps-why = "the smallest program that proves a board booted and reached its console", ps-in = ["OutDir"], ps-out = [hello-src-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s02-body }

Section: S03 -- Board Definitions

  s03-body : List ShellCmd =
    [ScBlank, ScRaw "$boards = @(\n    @{ Name = 'arm64';   Plug = 'arm64';  Compile = 'compile-arm64.ps1'; Board = 'codex-arm64.repl';   Expected = 'BOARD-TEST-OK' },\n    @{ Name = 'riscv64'; Plug = 'riscv';  Compile = 'compile-riscv.ps1'; Board = 'codex-riscv64.repl'; Expected = 'BOARD-TEST-OK' }\n)", ScBlank, ScIf (SeStringNeq (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "Arch") (SeLit "all")) [ScRaw "$boards = $boards | Where-Object { $_.Name -eq $Arch }"] [], ScBlank, ScRaw "$pass = 0; $fail = 0; $skip = 0"]

  s03 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "board definitions", ps-why = "the two boards, each naming its plug, its compile driver and the line its console must print", ps-in = ["Arch"], ps-out = [boards-art, pass-art, fail-art, skip-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s03-body }

Section: S04 -- Board Loop

  s04-compile : List ShellCmd =
    [ScAssign "elfOut" (SeRaw "Join-Path $OutDir \"hello-$($b.Name).elf\""), ScAssign "compileScript" (SeRaw "Join-Path $Repo \"codex\\plugs\\$($b.Plug)\\$($b.Compile)\""), ScBlank, ScRaw "Write-Host \"  $($b.Name): compiling...\" -NoNewline", ScRaw "$prev = $ErrorActionPreference; $ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'", ScRaw "& pwsh -NoProfile -File $compileScript -Src $HelloSrc -Out $elfOut 2>&1 | Out-Null", ScRaw "$ErrorActionPreference = $prev", ScIf (SeOr (SeNot (SeExitCodeEq 0)) (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "elfOut")))) [ScRaw "Write-Host \" FAIL (compile)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "$fail++; continue"] []]

  s04-renode : List ShellCmd =
    [ScAssign "uartLog" (SeRaw "Join-Path $OutDir \"uart-$($b.Name).log\""), ScIf (SeFileExists (SeVar "uartLog")) [ScDelete (SeVar "uartLog")] [], ScBlank, ScRaw "$elfPath = (Resolve-Path $elfOut).Path -replace '\\\\','/'", ScRaw "$boardPath = (Resolve-Path $boardRepl).Path -replace '\\\\','/'", ScRaw "$uartPath = $uartLog -replace '\\\\','/'", ScBlank, ScRaw "$rescLines = @(\n        'mach create \"codex\"'\n        \"machine LoadPlatformDescription @$boardPath\"\n        \"sysbus LoadELF @$elfPath\"\n        \"uart0 CreateFileBackend @$uartPath true\"\n        'start'\n        'sleep 3'\n        'quit'\n    )", ScAssign "rescFile" (SeRaw "Join-Path $OutDir \"test-$($b.Name).resc\""), ScDotNetCall "System.IO.File" "WriteAllLines" [SeVar "rescFile", SeVar "rescLines"], ScRaw "$rescPath = $rescFile -replace '\\\\','/'", ScBlank, ScRaw "$prev = $ErrorActionPreference; $ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'", ScRaw "& $RenodeExe --disable-xwt --console -e \"include @$rescPath\" 2>&1 | Out-Null", ScRaw "$ErrorActionPreference = $prev", ScRaw "Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500"]

  s04-verify : List ShellCmd =
    let pass-branch = [ScRaw "Write-Host \" PASS\" -ForegroundColor Green", ScRaw "$pass++"]
    in let fail-uart = [ScRaw "$preview = if ($uart) { $uart.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(60, $uart.Length)).Trim() } else { \"(empty)\" }", ScRaw "Write-Host \" FAIL (uart: $preview)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "$fail++"]
    in let no-log = [ScRaw "Write-Host \" FAIL (no uart log)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "$fail++"]
    in [ScIf (SeFileExists (SeVar "uartLog")) [ScRaw "$uart = Get-Content $uartLog -Raw -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue", ScIf (SeAnd (SeVar "uart") (SeRaw "$uart -match [regex]::Escape($b.Expected)")) pass-branch fail-uart] no-log]

  s04-body : List ShellCmd =
    let plug-skip = [ScRaw "Write-Host \"  SKIP  $($b.Name): plug not built ($plugCdx)\" -ForegroundColor Yellow", ScRaw "$skip++; continue"]
    in let board-skip = [ScRaw "Write-Host \"  SKIP  $($b.Name): board definition missing ($boardRepl)\" -ForegroundColor Yellow", ScRaw "$skip++; continue"]
    in [ScBlank, ScForEach "b" (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "boards") [ScAssign "plugCdx" (SeRaw "Join-Path $Repo \"codex\\plugs\\$($b.Plug)\\build-output\\$($b.Plug)-plug.cdx\""), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "plugCdx"))) plug-skip [], ScBlank, ScAssign "boardRepl" (SeRaw "Join-Path $Repo \"tools\\renode\\codex\\$($b.Board)\""), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "boardRepl"))) board-skip [], ScBlank, ScSequence s04-compile, ScBlank, ScSequence s04-renode, ScBlank, ScSequence s04-verify]]

 A MISSING PLUG OR BOARD IS A SKIP AND NOT A FAILURE, counted separately and
 reported, so a run where nothing was built prints three skips and exits zero.

  s04 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "board loop", ps-why = "per board: compile the hello program with its plug, boot it under Renode, and look for its line in the uart capture", ps-in = ["boards", "Repo", "OutDir", "HelloSrc", "RenodeExe"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [PrGuests 1], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s04-body }

Section: S05 -- Summary

  s05-body : List ShellCmd =
    [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit ""), ScRaw "Write-Host \"Board tests: $pass pass, $fail fail, $skip skip\" -ForegroundColor $(if ($fail -gt 0) { 'Red' } else { 'Green' })", ScExit (pipe-ref tb-arts testboards-params "fail")]

  s05 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "summary", ps-why = "report the three tallies and exit with the failure count, which PipeOutcome cannot spell", ps-in = ["pass", "fail", "skip"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoComputed "the number of board arms that failed, which is why a green run and a one-board failure are distinguishable by the code alone"], ps-body = s05-body }

Section: Assembly

  tb-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "test-boards", pl-doc = "Cross-architecture board tests via Renode", pl-params = testboards-params, pl-stages = [PsStage s01, PsStage s02, PsStage s03, PsStage s04, PsStage s05] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell tb-pipe))
  end

